{"step_index":73,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-30T16:52:46Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-30T22:22:46+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-30T22:22:51+05:30\nThe search for \"\"GTA\" \"Spider-Man\" \"Menyoo\" \"YouTube\" monetization site:reddit.com\" returned the following summary:\nThe intersection of using mods (like **Menyoo** for **GTA**), third-party intellectual property (like **Spider-Man**), and **YouTube monetization** is a complex topic often discussed in gaming communities on Reddit[1][2].\n\n### **Key Considerations Regarding Monetization**\n\n*   **The Nature of Copyright and IP:** Using a Spider-Man character model in *Grand Theft Auto* involves two distinct layers of intellectual property: Rockstar Games (GTA) and Marvel/Sony (Spider-Man)[2]. While gameplay footage is often tolerated by developers as \"free promotion,\" using prominent third-party IP (like Spider-Man) can increase the risk of copyright strikes because it involves assets that the game publisher does not own[3][2].\n*   **\"Fair Use\" vs. Legal Reality:** Many creators argue that transformative content (e.g., adding commentary, edits, or roleplay) falls under fair use[4][2]. However, Reddit discussions frequently highlight that **fair use is a legal defense, not a guarantee**[2]. Copyright holders (especially those protecting major brands like Marvel) have the right to issue takedowns regardless of whether the video is monetized[5][2].\n*   **Publisher Stance:**\n    *   **Rockstar Games:** Historically, Rockstar has had a mixed relationship with mods[6]. While they generally allow single-player modding, they have been known to take action against content they perceive as harmful to their brand or online ecosystem (e.g., specific GTA RP situations)[6].\n    *   **Monetization Risks:** Most advice on platforms like Reddit suggests that while many YouTubers monetize modded gameplay without issue, it remains a \"gray area\"[1][3]. The primary risk is not necessarily the mod itself, but receiving a copyright claim or strike from the IP holder[3][6].\n*   **Community Consensus:** \n    *   **Avoid Music:** Copyrighted music is a more common t\n<truncated 869 bytes>\nnformation is based on community discussions and general principles of copyright law; it does not constitute legal advice[2]. If you are concerned about your channel, consult the specific EULA/creator guidelines of the game and, if necessary, a legal professional[3][2].\n\nSources:\n[1] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHL9JeSeQZFkb5Nn2PG5pe0r-Me3BgtBUTKKHgkENj3B1AgwBTjbvyADt0UBVYN-AveTmExwRXxYxbEcav0KKP8I7bCMBNTG8FA8CPGBhqel3mGXeP9ZQhmH3GCijxjyxKaPEt59cGZyynTOjCKN0FeRjr_s_bKA-hgTjvwuC0tDgLFtq8e1jg0q6IU45aK-YpZkA5o_yOhxh07K3-pfw==)\n[2] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFNtPQbO5GUfl0TQF_T89mAYyNPzA9F2HF_DE-JmeAmgkZtJ7FpK5RtmIf47OuhqIOT62TDOHUVvnf-DNkJT-kHUUQ6jvvr0U-ez2RAwsyWxPO_lqcEMvk1hxvm226GyjLH0GSa6af9MJijiPGI01g7JsrVOAV4igH7oXlZ6FdKFGVsP_F24yI8o1UzgM22YQU8Gur4LxXj)\n[3] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH83CQK2gEnexshRFa7f6YrWsQ451XdWiHw3ndlZPvp3FCWoruHrKWyxTTGCGFqzW-_fzj4mKj5Y-Vmika6pniDEXr4Ghn-Z8QMjLnB4XW1N5R7aLkMp7rp5LqZtVV4akh_VnFp-NfpVERa6EztwG6rZQKW-4nR2cl5Dp6Q6Di7LPZuq0eIkox_XbPUhBZ7gJhwUWU4bCEol32K_g==)\n[4] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH8a6v3wZQUv5NSXwJKWiDozIzuc3PNn204a3dj1uuWQXtucY9-pgQ_qs3Xca2d1EiLYTIl5TlUOxZYt2cJvOp8euAL6fPcttv0fUVCJJaQEgxaOhArjDxR9I2qmtc54ITvse8MEBfV6-TjZHY9IqyPpuCagSuBzpMFm0s9mGaHvWdCmoPAk1rTwyh-_wCkpsXcoQbkoU38xdrCig==)\n[5] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGTLYRYq7TL8MUABaD2uTuNFEVU0Cs1ErB7ieMaj1UJM9pqLFA1Tw0qkX0pLU6NX-RcypHyTGq5APAAbhCCGgvcSXoPoxGMHBQhYURon1-xGEaSlhDhDSqNID9C_QtDpI8kUhvYbC-ed3jyhT12vo42ANneUcz2gfbygx7ahMQsXUsBzXmGStpAEa0b-NZ3rYRbn4TXfecF)\n[6] [reddit.com](